#====================================================================
# DRAFT-conan-cmake-test-fixture-prefetch — CMake configure-time raw test data
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-conan-cmake-test-fixture-prefetch
trigger_tool:           cmake|conan
phase:                  source|configuration
error_signature:        file\(DOWNLOAD\).*scap_files|conan create.*TIMED OUT|Configuring done.*3600

severity:               2
category:               network, build-system, cmake, conan, testing
match_keywords:         file(DOWNLOAD), CMAKE_BINARY_DIR, scap_files, test fixture, Conan source, SHA256, configure-time, offline CI, upstream tests, S3 path-style, TLS EOF
title:                  "CMake configure-time download assets: Conan source acquisition and build-directory staging"

root_cause:             Some CMake projects keep real upstream tests enabled but download binary test fixtures with file(DOWNLOAD) while configuring; URL-driven ExternalProject dependencies can fail at the same boundary even when the main source is correct. A clean CI worker can fetch the package source yet stall in configure or the first build step on each asset; disabling the suite would hide the original test denominator. The inputs need the same checksum-bound acquisition and staging boundary as other Conan sources, while the upstream test registration remains unchanged.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for CMake projects whose test targets use file(DOWNLOAD) or whose bundled dependencies use URL-driven ExternalProject downloads for raw data/source archives, and whose upstream CMake checks files below CMAKE_BINARY_DIR or <name>-prefix/src before building those targets.
verification_cmd:       grep -RnE 'file\\(DOWNLOAD|CMAKE_BINARY_DIR.*/(fixtures|scap_files)' <source>; conan create <recipe> --profile:host <ohos-profile> --profile:build <ohos-profile>; inspect the configure log for staged assets and zero fixture downloads; run the complete upstream suite and test_package

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            conan-source-checksummed-asset-and-build-staging
rec_description:        Record every official asset URL and SHA256 in recipe constants; use Conan tools.files.download() in source() to acquire each file with checksum verification; before CMake configure, copy raw test fixtures into CMAKE_BINARY_DIR/scap_files and URL-driven ExternalProject archives into the exact <name>-prefix/src location that CMake probes. Keep the upstream test option and registration enabled, and report raw static, registered, runner, executed, skipped, and consumer counts independently.
rec_command:            "conanfile.py SCAP_FILES/BUNDLED_SOURCES; source(): download(..., sha256=...); if the official virtual-host S3 endpoint has TLS EOF, verify the official path-style endpoint for the same object; build(): copy verified files to Path(self.build_folder)/scap_files or Path(self.build_folder)/<prefix>-prefix/src/<filename> before CMake(self).configure()"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upstream-option-or-approved-local-source
fallback_description:   If the upstream provides a real fixture-source directory override, use that override only with an approved checksum-verified source tree. If it provides a switch that disables only nonessential fixture tests, record the exact unregistered denominator; never turn off the entire upstream suite to conceal a configure fetch failure.
fallback_command:       cmake -D<upstream_fixture_source_dir>=<approved-source> <source>; ctest --output-on-failure
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual

forbid_1_pattern:       BUILD_TESTING.*OFF.*(fixture|file\\(DOWNLOAD)|upstream.*test)|skip.*scap.*fixture.*and.*report.*pass
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling the upstream suite or silently excluding fixture cases removes the validation layer instead of making its inputs reproducible.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package may compile while the reported upstream denominator is false, and CI cannot detect regressions covered by the original fixture suite.

forbid_2_pattern:       fixture.*download.*without.*sha256|copy.*fixture.*without.*source\(\)|local.*fixture.*embedded.*binary
forbid_2_reason:        Unchecked or repository-embedded binary data is not an auditable Conan input and can drift between workers or exceed the archive review boundary.
forbid_2_consequence:   A green local build does not prove that CI used the intended test data or that the fixture contents match the upstream release.

principles:             P002, P003, P014
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             E299, E342, E377, DRAFT-isutf8-cmake-configure-download-benchmarks
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

